<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://w3id.org/hacid/onto/ccso#"
     xml:base="https://w3id.org/hacid/onto/ccso"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:top="https://w3id.org/hacid/onto/top-level/"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:dcat="http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:terms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hacid/onto/ccso">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/hacid/onto/ccso/2.0/"/>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/hacid/onto/data"/>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/hacid/onto/top-level"/>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/hacid/onto/core/judgement"/>
        <dc:description rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hacid-project/knowledge-graph/main/ontologies/climate-services/visual/simpler_model_rev.png"/>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/hacid/data/cs/person/andrea-giovanni-nuzzolese"/>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/hacid/data/cs/person/miguel-ceriani"/>
        <terms:title xml:lang="en">CCSO - Core Climate Services Ontology</terms:title>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The Core Climate Services Ontology (CCSO) is a comprehensive framework designed to facilitate the representation and integration of diverse climate-related data and knowledge. This ontology encompasses key concepts related to climate models, simulations, datasets, variables, and scenarios, along with their associated characteristics. The CCSO enables structured and standardized descriptions of these elements, promoting interoperability and data sharing among various stakeholders in climate science.

Key features of the ontology include definitions of object properties such as spatial and temporal coverage, spatial and temporal resolution, and the relationships between simulations, datasets, climate models, and scenarios. These relationships are crucial for linking datasets with the variables they contain, the models used to generate climate projections, and the scenarios that guide simulation experiments.

The ontology also categorizes different types of scenarios, such as Greenhouse Gas Concentration Pathways and Shared Socioeconomic Pathways, which are essential for modeling and predicting the impacts of various emission trajectories on the climate system. By providing a clear and systematic way to describe and relate these complex elements, the CCSO aims to enhance the understanding, analysis, and dissemination of climate data, ultimately supporting more informed decision-making in climate research and policy.

Overall, the Core Climate Services Ontology serves as a vital tool for organizing climate knowledge, facilitating data interoperability, and advancing the study and application of climate science.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CCSO - Core Climate Services Ontology</rdfs:label>
        <dcat:keyword xml:lang="en">climate model simulations</dcat:keyword>
        <dcat:keyword xml:lang="en">climate models</dcat:keyword>
        <dcat:keyword xml:lang="en">climate services</dcat:keyword>
        <dcat:keyword xml:lang="en">climate variables</dcat:keyword>
        <dcat:theme xml:lang="en">Climate services</dcat:theme>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


